#What is Schema?
→ Database schema describes the structure of each table and the datatype that each column of the table can contain.
  :- for ex. In Movies database , the values in the year column must be - Integer
                                , the values in the title column must be - String/text in datatype.
#Inserting New data
## Query
  - INSERT INTO mytable
  - VALUES (value_or_expr, another_value_or_expr, ...),
           (value_or_expr_2, another_value_or_expr_2, ...)

#When data is incomplete and column supports default values
 ##Query
    -INSERT INTO mytable
    - (column, another_column,...)
    - (value_or_expr, another_value_or_expr,...),
  (value_or_expr_2, another_value_or_expr_2, ...),
        .....;

Example:-
